{
  "$schema": "../../schema/markup.schema.json",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "id": "contact-form",
  "kind": "component",
  "root": {
    "element": "form",
    "classes": [
      "salt-contact__form"
    ],
    "attributes": {
      "id": "from:form id (salt-contact-<n>)",
      "method": "post",
      "action": "from:platform endpoint",
      "novalidate": ""
    },
    "note": "The action is platform-native (SC-003); the markup is not."
  },
  "elements": [
    {
      "role": "field",
      "element": "div",
      "classes": [
        "salt-contact__field"
      ],
      "repeat": {
        "from": "name, email, phone (when asked), enquiry type (two or more types), message"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "role": "label",
          "element": "label",
          "classes": [
            "salt-contact__label"
          ],
          "attributes": {
            "for": "from:field id"
          },
          "text": "from:labels.<field>",
          "children": [
            {
              "role": "optional",
              "element": "span",
              "classes": [
                "salt-contact__optional"
              ],
              "text": "from:labels.optional",
              "optional": true,
              "when": "phone is optional"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "error",
          "element": "p",
          "classes": [
            "salt-contact__error"
          ],
          "attributes": {
            "id": "from:field id-error"
          },
          "text": "from:error",
          "optional": true,
          "when": "the field failed validation"
        },
        {
          "role": "input",
          "element": [
            "input",
            "select",
            "textarea"
          ],
          "classes": [
            "salt-contact__input"
          ],
          "attributes": {
            "id": "from:field id",
            "name": "from:field name",
            "required": {
              "value": "",
              "when": "the field is required"
            },
            "aria-invalid": {
              "value": "true",
              "when": "error"
            },
            "aria-describedby": {
              "value": "from:error id and status id",
              "when": "error or challenge"
            },
            "autocomplete": {
              "enum": [
                "name",
                "email",
                "tel"
              ]
            }
          },
          "note": "textarea rows=6 for the message."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "challenge",
      "element": "div",
      "classes": [
        "salt-contact__field"
      ],
      "optional": true,
      "when": "the anti-spam credentials were issued. When a captcha provider is configured, the provider's widget is native, and this challenge is drawn inside a noscript element",
      "children": [
        {
          "role": "challenge-label",
          "element": "label",
          "classes": [
            "salt-contact__label"
          ],
          "attributes": {
            "for": "from:field id"
          },
          "text": "from:challenge.question"
        },
        {
          "role": "challenge-error",
          "element": "p",
          "classes": [
            "salt-contact__error"
          ],
          "optional": true,
          "when": "the answer failed"
        },
        {
          "role": "challenge-input",
          "element": "input",
          "classes": [
            "salt-contact__input",
            "salt-contact__input--short"
          ],
          "attributes": {
            "type": "text",
            "inputmode": "numeric",
            "autocomplete": "off",
            "required": "",
            "aria-describedby": "from:status id"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "hidden",
      "element": "input",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "hidden",
        "name": "from:token and return fields"
      },
      "repeat": {
        "from": "challenge token, form token, return path"
      }
    },
    {
      "role": "trap",
      "element": "div",
      "classes": [
        "salt-sr-only",
        "salt-contact__trap"
      ],
      "attributes": {
        "aria-hidden": "true"
      },
      "note": "Honeypot: label + text input with tabindex -1, autocomplete off."
    },
    {
      "role": "privacy",
      "element": "p",
      "classes": [
        "salt-contact__privacy"
      ],
      "optional": true,
      "when": "a privacy page is set",
      "children": [
        {
          "role": "privacy-link",
          "element": "a",
          "attributes": {
            "href": "from:privacy page url"
          },
          "text": "from:labels.privacy"
        }
      ],
      "note": "The sentence around the link comes from labels.privacyLine."
    },
    {
      "role": "actions",
      "element": "div",
      "classes": [
        "salt-contact__actions"
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "role": "submit",
          "component": "button",
          "classes": [
            "salt-contact__submit"
          ],
          "attributes": {
            "type": "submit",
            "data-style": "primary"
          },
          "text": "from:labels.submit"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "status",
      "element": "p",
      "classes": [
        "salt-contact__status"
      ],
      "attributes": {
        "id": "from:status id",
        "role": "status",
        "aria-live": "polite",
        "tabindex": "-1",
        "data-tone": {
          "enum": [
            "sending",
            "sent",
            "problem"
          ],
          "when": "a status is shown"
        }
      },
      "text": "from:status.message",
      "note": "Always present so the live region exists before it speaks; focused after a send."
    }
  ],
  "headings": {
    "provides": "never",
    "level": "none"
  },
  "zeroState": "Drawn whenever the site accepts enquiries; otherwise the contact section draws its closed message instead.",
  "dataAttributes": [
    {
      "name": "data-tone",
      "on": "status",
      "values": [
        "sending",
        "sent",
        "problem"
      ],
      "when": "after a submission"
    }
  ],
  "script": {
    "kind": "progressive",
    "withoutScript": "A native POST to the platform's endpoint that redirects back with the status.",
    "withScript": "Submits in place, fetches the anti-spam credentials (or, with a captcha provider, the provider's token), fills the status region and moves focus to it."
  },
  "uses": [
    "button"
  ],
  "ruleRefs": [
    "section#focus-ring",
    "section#target-size",
    "section#sr-only"
  ],
  "hooks": [
    {
      "class": "salt-contact__trap",
      "role": "trap",
      "reason": "Identifies the honeypot; salt-sr-only hides it."
    },
    {
      "class": "salt-contact__actions",
      "role": "actions",
      "reason": "The submit row; laid out by the form's gap."
    },
    {
      "class": "salt-contact__submit",
      "role": "submit",
      "reason": "Names the submit button for scripts and tests; salt-button styles it."
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    {
      "topic": "stylesheet-owes",
      "text": "The privacy line, from WordPress (SC-006); no rule yet.",
      "classes": [
        "salt-contact__privacy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "ruling",
      "text": "The form shows a privacy line when a privacy page is set (SC-006). When a captcha provider is configured, its widget is native and the arithmetic challenge is drawn inside noscript, so a visitor without JavaScript can still send the form: the challenge's credentials exist when the page is drawn, and a correct answer is accepted in place of a provider token. How each platform issues and checks them is native form delivery (SC-003). SC-006 accepts that the arithmetic path stays open beside a captcha. Without a provider the challenge is drawn as it is."
    },
    {
      "topic": "ruling",
      "text": "Field names in the markup are the contract's; each platform maps them to its handler (SC-003)."
    }
  ],
  "platforms": {
    "nextjs": {
      "owes": [
        "The privacy line when a privacy page is set, and the arithmetic challenge inside noscript when a captcha provider is configured (SC-006)."
      ]
    },
    "wordpress": {
      "formerly": [
        {
          "role": "root",
          "element": "form",
          "classes": [
            "x-contact-form",
            "flex",
            "w-full",
            "flex-col",
            "gap-4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "status",
          "element": "div",
          "classes": [
            "x-contact-status"
          ],
          "attributes": [
            "id=salt-contact-form",
            "role=status",
            "aria-live=polite",
            "data-salt-contact-status"
          ],
          "note": "Before the form today; a div holding a p."
        },
        {
          "role": "input",
          "element": "input",
          "note": "names salt_contact_name, salt_contact_email, salt_contact_message, salt_contact_type; honeypot salt_hp; time trap salt_time"
        }
      ],
      "owes": [
        "Field, label, error and status markup as above; status after the actions, inside the form; phone field per the site setting; one id per form (salt-contact-<n>) instead of a static id.",
        "The privacy line as p.salt-contact__privacy before the actions (SC-006)."
      ]
    }
  }
}
